      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gilmanton%2C_New_Hampshire",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s first school, Gilmanton Academy, was founded in 1794 as one of the state’s earliest academies.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gilmanton%2C_New_Hampshire",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Gilmanton Iron Works, once called Averytown, preserves an 18th‑century iron‑mining village along the Suncook River.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7,
        19
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2",
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://localnh.com/towns/gilmanton",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The historic Gilmanton Ironworks Library, built 1916‑17, is the county’s first Colonial Revival library building.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://localnh.com/towns/gilmanton",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Gilmanton Corner hosts the 1840 Isaac Smith Meeting House, the town’s oldest standing church building.",
